<title>BRAZIL: Brazil Central Bank sells dollar-indexed notes.</title>
<headline>Brazil Central Bank sells dollar-indexed notes.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's Central Bank sold Monday a total face value of 500 million reais in dollar-indexed special series of Central Bank Notes (NBC-E), dealers said.</p>
<p>The notes, which have mature in six months and expire on September 4, 1997, will pay an annual yield of 11.41 percent plus the variation of the foreign exchange rate in the period, they added.</p>
<p>((-- Romina Nicaretta, Sao Paulo newsroom, 55 11 248 5418))</p>
